> AGB_Hack is an adaptation of Don Kneller's PC Hack 3.61 to the GameBoy
> Advance.
>
> New features:
>
> * Menu-based inventory/command interface. You can now select an object
> in your inventory and perform actions relevant to it. For example:
>
> a +1 leather armor (being worn)
> ...Take Off
> ...Drop
> ...Throw
> ...Name
>
> * Many selections that previously required a keypress have been
> converted to menus.
>
> * Bugfixes, optimizations and small changes to improve playability
> (see changes.txt file for details)
>
> Like the last version, saved games are stored as a set of sequential
> keystrokes that return the game to a previous state. In other words,
> you have to wait for your game to play itself back from the start; it
> does go pretty quickly, though. I had to do it this way because of the
> very limited memory of the GBA.
>
> >From testing, it seems there is just enough memory available for a
>
> complete winning game in which the player visits 30 persistent levels.
> Any more risks a "dungeon collapse". Maybe with a higher compression
> algorithm I could squeeze in a few more.
